{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NxweQq8kvKsT32ERh2aspC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"e5731c9447e62b0751fafbd37198b7d76558218e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-07T20:02:47+06:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5850: Support concept reference ranges in the Angular form engine (#3546)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5850: Apply concept reference ranges in the AMPATH form engine\\n\\nThe AMPATH form engine only ever derived the bounds of a numeric question\\nfrom questionOptions.min / questionOptions.max in the form schema, so the\\npatient specific reference ranges added in Platform 2.7 were never taken\\ninto account. A form could happily accept a value the backend then rejects.\\n\\nThe wrapper now fetches the ranges for the concepts of all numeric\\nquestions from /conceptreferencerange before the form is built, and\\nnarrows each question to the absolute bounds of the range that applies to\\nthe patient. A bound already set by the schema is never widened, the\\nstricter of the two wins. Only the absolute bounds are used, which is what\\nthe backend validates against too.\\n\\nIf the ranges cannot be fetched (older backends do not have the resource,\\nand there is nothing to fetch while offline) the form loads unconstrained,\\nexactly as before.\\n\\n* (fix) O3-5850: Page and bound the concept reference range request\\n\\nTwo problems with fetching every concept in one unbounded request.\\n\\nThe resource is paged, and REST defaults to 50 results, so a form with\\nmore than 50 numeric concepts silently lost the ranges of everything past\\nthe first page. Each request now follows its next link until the backend\\nruns out of pages.\\n\\nA single concept the backend cannot resolve also used to take the whole\\nform down with it, since catchError turned any failure into an empty map.\\nConcepts are now resolved and deduplicated against the schema's\\nconceptReferences before the request, so references known not to resolve\\nare never sent, and the remainder goes out in bounded batches. A batch\\nthat still fails costs only its own ranges.\\n\\n* Update packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-schema/concept-reference-ranges.ts\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\n\\n* Update packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-schema/concept-reference-ranges.ts\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\n\\n* Update packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-schema/concept-reference-ranges.spec.ts\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\\n\\n* (test) O3-5850: Cover the shapes conceptReferences actually takes\\n\\nThe omitted-key tests only covered mappings, so nothing pinned down what\\nhappens to a raw UUID. o3forms keys conceptReferences by the reference the\\nquestion uses, UUIDs included, so a UUID that resolves is present as its own\\nkey and one that doesn't is absent. Both now have a test, along with the\\nolder backends that send no conceptReferences at all.\\n\\nAlso drops the `uuid: null` shape from the remaining test, since o3forms\\nnever emits it.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Md Nahid Hassan Bhuiyan\",\"authorEmail\":\"70757745+Nahid-NHB@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T22:50:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d47d346cc105c4c72dfb1ce68a05abbcb1ad4f84\",\"date\":\"2026-06-10T15:22:43+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Deduplicate overlapping test result branches in the results viewer (#3374)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f\",\"date\":\"2026-06-10T07:24:55+01:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) De-duplicate repeated lab results in the test results viewer (#3345)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Tests results: dedupe lab results by conceptUuid to stop duplicate rows\\n\\nProblem\\nOn the patient-chart lab results viewer, a single lab result is rendered\\nmultiple times — once per order placed for that test. A NEW order plus its\\nauto-generated DISCONTINUE order made the same result show twice; two orders,\\nfour times, and so on.\\n\\nRoot cause\\nThe /obstree backend returns the same orderable-test concept under several\\nbranches of the orderable-tests tree (effectively one branch per order), each\\nbranch carrying the same single observation. In filter-context's tableData\\nbuilder the de-duplication key is based on test.flatName, which differs per\\nbranch, so the identical observation is not collapsed and renders once per\\nbranch.\\n\\nFix\\nKey the de-duplication on the observation's conceptUuid instead of flatName.\\nThe same observation (same concept + datetime + value) reached via different\\nbranches now collapses to a single row, while genuinely different tests stay\\nseparate. One-line change, no new dependencies, no new i18n keys.\\n\\n* (fix) Scope lab results dedupe to the rendered panel, not just conceptUuid\\n\\nKeying de-duplication on conceptUuid alone collapsed the same observation\\nacross different rendered panels. A concept mounted under two roots (e.g.\\nPlatelets under both Hematology and Bloodwork) was deduped to a single row,\\ndropping the tree view from 3 tables to 2 and Platelets from 2 rows to 1.\\n\\nScope the dedupe key to the panel group key derived from flatName, so the\\nsame concept that legitimately appears under different panels stays as\\nseparate rows while true duplicates within one panel still collapse. Extract\\nthe group-key derivation into a shared helper used by both the dedupe and the\\ngrouping step so the two scopes stay aligned.\\n\\nAdd regression tests covering both directions: collapse within one panel and\\nkeep across two panels.\\n\\n\\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"cerveaubleu64\",\"authorEmail\":\"50305875+cerveaubleu64@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a361874c505e887692338db4d52bb4367e0f448d\",\"date\":\"2026-02-17T20:51:31+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5435: Fix TypeError when launching lab order workspace from form engine (#3032)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The form engine's workspace-launcher opens the add-lab-order workspace\\nwithout passing orderTypeUuid in workspaceProps. This caused .find() to\\nreturn undefined when looking up the order type, and accessing\\n.orderableConceptSets on undefined threw a TypeError.\\n\\nMake orderTypeUuid optional and fall back to the configured\\norders.labOrderTypeUuid default. Also deduplicate the\\nAddTestOrderWorkspaceProps interface that was duplicated across the\\ninternal and exported workspace wrappers.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":5}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e52182a-12d6-4bbb-99b4-1e875bda2315","uuid":"4ea71dac-fa0f-46b3-97bf-080b1dcc68a5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:55:36.573Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"e5731c9447e62b0751fafbd37198b7d76558218e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-07T20:02:47+06:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5850: Support concept reference ranges in the Angular form engine (#3546)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) O3-5850: Apply concept reference ranges in the AMPATH form engine\\n\\nThe AMPATH form engine only ever derived the bounds of a numeric question\\nfrom questionOptions.min / questionOptions.max in the form schema, so the\\npatient specific reference ranges added in Platform 2.7 were never taken\\ninto account. A form could happily accept a value the backend then rejects.\\n\\nThe wrapper now fetches the ranges for the concepts of all numeric\\nquestions from /conceptreferencerange before the form is built, and\\nnarrow