{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKMySg9aexGuWDqRWxKp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The change is commit `d47d346` (PR #3374, \"Deduplicate overlapping test result branches in the results viewer\"), which follows up #3345 (`16600fb`). I could not find the ticket. The server-side change is only implied in code comments: the reducer says identity should come from obs UUIDs \"until the backend exposes obs uuids.\" No commit, PR body, or indexed file names a ticket key for it, so I have left the ticket out rather than guess.\n\n**How the de-duplication was reworked**\n\n- **Before:** #3345 keyed de-duplication on `conceptUuid` plus panel group, then `obsDatetime` and `value`. Its commit body says the obstree returns the same concept under several branches, one per order. The branch-level obs lists were concatenated, so the same result was counted once per branch.\n- **Reducer (`d47d346`):** `INITIALIZE` no longer concatenates duplicate-`flatName` obs lists. It merges them with `mergeObsMultisetMax`, which keeps the highest count of each `obsDatetime|value` identity across copies. Equal obs within one list stay distinct. Nodes are copied so the SWR-cached trees are not mutated.\n- **Context (`d47d346`):** a new `normalizedTests` memo groups rendered branches by panel group plus concept. It merges their obs with the same multiset-max rule. `tableData`, `timelineData`, `totalResultsCount` and `filteredResultsCount` all derive from it, so the header count matches the rows. Entries carry a `flatNames` array so checkbox filtering still works for collapsed branches.\n- **Limitation (documented in the code):** `obsDatetime` plus `value` cannot tell a copy from a real duplicate that only appears in separate lists. The comment says this is left as-is until the backend exposes obs UUIDs.\n\n**Server-side change the ticket proposes:** per the reducer comment, the backend would expose obs UUIDs in the `/obstree` response so clients can match copies by identity rather than by datetime and value. I could not confirm this in the webservices or core repositories, and a `RESTWS-998` commit in `openmrs-module-webservices.rest` is only about interpretation and reference ranges.\n\n**Evidence, best first**\n\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.ts` lines 11–39: `mergeObsMultisetMax` and the limitation comment.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.ts` lines 129–141: `INITIALIZE` dedupe using the multiset merge.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx` lines 112–155: `normalizedTests` memo.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx` lines 224–232: `tableData` built from `normalizedTests`.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.test.ts` lines 590–640: tests for collapsing copies, keeping repeated equal obs within one list, and idempotence.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.test.tsx` lines 574–728: tests for the header count and for two distinct equal-value results rendering as two rows.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/tree-view/tree-view.component.tsx` lines 31–36: `entryMatchesCheckbox`, which matches checkboxes against all collapsed `flatNames`.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/tree-view/tree-view.test.tsx` lines 111–167: checkbox filtering of collapsed duplicate branches.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/types.ts` lines 191–192: the `flatNames` field on `MappedObservation`.\n- `openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/grouped-timeline/grouped-timeline.component.tsx` lines 26–30: panel matching by `flatNames`.\n- Commit `openmrs-esm-patient-chart` `d47d346cc105c4c72dfb1ce68a05abbcb1ad4f84`: the reworked de-duplication (PR #3374).\n- Commit `openmrs-esm-patient-chart` `16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f`: the earlier conceptUuid/panel-scoped de-duplication, with the root-cause description (PR #3345).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.ts\", \"startLine\": 11, \"endLine\": 39},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.ts\", \"startLine\": 129, \"endLine\": 141},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx\", \"startLine\": 112, \"endLine\": 155},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx\", \"startLine\": 224, \"endLine\": 232},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 590, \"endLine\": 640},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 574, \"endLine\": 728},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/tree-view/tree-view.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 31, \"endLine\": 36},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/tree-view/tree-view.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 111, \"endLine\": 167},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/types.ts\", \"startLine\": 191, \"endLine\": 192},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/grouped-timeline/grouped-timeline.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 26, \"endLine\": 30},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-ch